---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icons from "../../components/Icons.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "../../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Forbidden City vs Summer Palace: Which Should You Visit?" description="Forbidden City or Summer Palace? Compare history, scale, crowds, time needed, and the experience of each of Beijing's two great imperial sites. Honest verdict for every traveler type.">
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: "Compare", href: "/#compare-guides" }, { label: "Forbidden City vs Summer Palace" }]} />
  <div class="relative py-24 md:py-32 overflow-hidden -mt-[68px]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center" style="background-image:url('/images/attractions/summer-palace.webp')"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#0a3b36]/88"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 text-center">
      <span class="tag tag-glass mb-4">Compare & Decide</span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl">Forbidden City vs Summer Palace</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 mx-auto max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/80">The two grandest imperial sites in Beijing — but they reward you in completely different ways.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12 pb-6">
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#0f766e] pl-5 py-2 rounded-r bg-[#ccfbf1]/30">
      <p class="text-base text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">The short answer:</strong> Visit the <strong>Forbidden City</strong> for imperial power, architecture, and 500 years of dynastic history — it is the essential Beijing sight. Visit the <strong>Summer Palace</strong> for beauty, lakeside calm, and the imperial family's leisure life. If you only have one day for imperial China, do the Forbidden City in the morning and Jingshan for the panorama; if you have two days, add the Summer Palace as a relaxed second-day escape.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Side-by-Side Comparison</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-[#d5d0c4] rounded-xl">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-[#f8f7f4] text-[#5c5a4c] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">
          <tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Feature</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Forbidden City</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Summer Palace</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">What it is</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Imperial palace complex</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Imperial garden & lake</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Scale</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">180 acres, ~980 buildings</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">716 acres (290 ha), lake dominates</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Ticket</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">CNY 40-60 (booked 7 days ahead)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">CNY 20-30 (walk-in)</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Time needed</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">3-4 hours minimum</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">3-4 hours (relaxed)</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Crowds</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Very heavy on central axis</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Moderate, spread out</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Highlights</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Three great halls, treasure galleries, imperial garden</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Long Corridor, Kunming Lake, Tower of Buddhist Incense, Marble Boat</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Best for</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">History, architecture, first-timers</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Landscape beauty, boat rides, relaxing</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Mood</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Monumental, formal</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Serene, romantic</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Booking</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Mandatory online, passport number</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Walk-in OK, small ID check</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">The Core Difference</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#d5d0c4]/40 p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-2">The Forbidden City is about power</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed">The palace was built to awe — the vast ceremonial courtyards, the raised marble platforms, the golden roofs that no commoner's building could approach. You experience history standing upright, dwarfed by scale, walking the exact stones 24 emperors walked. It is architecture as government: every axis, every number of roof ridges, every bronze vessel arranged to communicate imperial authority. This is the place to understand how China was ruled for 500 years.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#d5d0c4]/40 p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-2">The Summer Palace is about pleasure</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed">The garden was built to soothe — a hill and lake composed as a painting, designed for strolls, boat rides, and imperial leisure. Empress Dowager Cixi poured funds into rebuilding it because this was where she escaped the palace's formality. You experience it with your body relaxed: the breeze off Kunming Lake, the painted beams of the Long Corridor overhead, the lake opening out as you climb. It is landscape architecture as art, and it asks you to slow down.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Which One Is Right for You?</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="users" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">First trip to China?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">The Forbidden City. It is the single most important site in Beijing and the one everyone expects you to have seen. Book tickets 7 days out.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="heart" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Traveling with kids?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">The Summer Palace wins — children under 18 enter free, the wide lakeside paths suit strollers, and a pedal boat on Kunming Lake beats walking formal courtyards. The Forbidden City is fine but harder work for little legs.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="clock" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Short on time?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Forbidden City first. It takes the same half-day as the Summer Palace but delivers more history per hour. Summer Palace can be compressed to a lake cruise + Long Corridor walk in 2 hours.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="star" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Want the best photos?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Summer Palace for landscape shots (lake + pagoda at golden hour); Forbidden City for architectural symmetry and the rooftop ocean from Jingshan. Both deliver; they just shoot differently.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8 border-t border-[#edeae3] pt-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Our Verdict by Traveler Type</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-[#d5d0c4] rounded-xl">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-[#f8f7f4] text-[#5c5a4c] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">
          <tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">If you are...</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Pick</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">First-time Beijing visitor</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Forbidden City</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">The essential, unmissable site</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Traveling with kids</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Summer Palace</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Free entry, boat rides, open space</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">History buff</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Forbidden City</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">500 years of dynastic story in situ</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Want to relax</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Summer Palace</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Lake, gardens, slow strolls</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Photographer</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Both</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Architecture vs landscape — do both</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">On a tight schedule</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Forbidden City</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">More history per hour</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Can You Do Both in One Day?</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed mb-4">Yes, comfortably — they are a natural pair. Start at the Forbidden City at opening (8:30am), walk the central axis plus one side gallery, exit the north gate into Jingshan for the panorama, then take Line 4 or a taxi to the Summer Palace (about 40 minutes) for a relaxed lake-and-Long-Corridor afternoon. It is a full but rewarding day, and the contrast between the two moods makes each more memorable.</p>
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#fef3c7] border border-[#d4a373]/30 p-6">
      <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">The honest bottom line:</strong> neither replaces the other. The Forbidden City is the reason you came to Beijing; the Summer Palace is the reason you enjoy it. If your itinerary forces a choice, choose the Forbidden City — then come back for the garden.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
